        "code": "// Day 53 Part 4: Distributed Multi-Hop Context Propagation Simulator\nclass DistributedServiceHopSimulator {\n  simulateHop(incomingTraceparent: string, serviceName: string): { outgoingTraceparent: string; hopLog: string } {\n    const parts = incomingTraceparent.split('-');\n    const traceId = parts[1];\n    const newSpanId = 'span_' + serviceName.toLowerCase();\n    const outgoing = '00-' + traceId + '-' + newSpanId + '-01';\n    const hopLog = '[' + serviceName + '] Propagated Trace: ' + traceId.slice(0, 8) + '... -> New Span: ' + newSpanId;\n    return { outgoingTraceparent: outgoing, hopLog };\n  }\n}\n\nconst simulator = new DistributedServiceHopSimulator();\nconst hop1 = simulator.simulateHop('00-4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736-00f067aa0ba902b7-01', 'AuthService');\nconst hop2 = simulator.simulateHop(hop1.outgoingTraceparent, 'PaymentService');\n\nconsole.log(hop1.hopLog);\nconsole.log(hop2.hopLog);\nconsole.log('Distributed Service Hop Context Propagation Verified: True');",
        "example": "Imagine an Olympic 4x100-meter relay race. The baton passed between the runners represents the W3C Trace Context. Runner one (the API Gateway) runs the first leg of the race and hands the baton smoothly to runner two (the AuthService). Runner two carries the exact same baton through the second turn and hands it to runner three (the PaymentService). Every runner runs their own individual leg of the race (their own Span), but the baton (the Trace ID) unites all four legs into a single coordinated championship race.",
